{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And the men who brought up an evil report of the land died.</b> Their tongues stretched out to their navels, etc. For it is said (Psalms 58:4): ״זֹרוּ רְשָׁעִים מֵרָחֶם תָּעוּ מִבֶּטֶן דֹּבְרֵי כָזָב״, and the infant, when it is in its mother's womb, then the navel stands in the place of the mouth, for its mouth is closed and its navel is open. And since even in the womb they went astray speaking lies — it is as though even in their mother's womb their mouths were open to speak lies and falsehood, and there the navel is in place of the mouth — therefore their tongues stretched out to their navels, because with every mouth they ate and consumed the land with their lying tongue. And the punishment was visible in these two places, for they are the place of the sin." "Another matter: because the land of Israel is called ״טַבּוּר הָאָרֶץ״ (Ezekiel 38:12), for it is in the middle of the settled world like the navel that is in the middle of the body — therefore the punishment was visible in the place of their navel, because they spread an evil report about this land that sits upon the navel of the earth."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The opening phrase 'their tongues stretched out to their navels, etc.' paraphrases the Talmudic midrash (Sotah 35a) that the spies' tongues swelled and extended to their navels, from which worms emerged; the 'etc.' (כו׳) gestures to the rest of that passage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:41:15.431597443Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}